        "answer": "SHA-256 (Secure Hash Algorithm 256-bit) is a cryptographic hash function that produces a fixed 64-character hexadecimal string representing any input data. It is widely used in password storage, digital certificates, file checksum integrity verification, and blockchain technologies."
